# Lines tools/qemu-test (and make check-serial, on the Pi 5) must see, in
# this order, as whole serial lines. Each USB host PD
# identifies its xHCI controller, halts and resets it, runs it from its own
# DMA region and has a No Op command come back through DMA. What differs by
# board - the controller's version and ports, the PCI placement on QEMU, what
# the firmware left running, what is attached - is printed between these
# lines and not checked.
NOWAYOS: usb0: starting
NOWAYOS: usb0: controller identified
NOWAYOS: usb0: halted and reset
NOWAYOS: usb0: running: a No Op command came back through DMA
NOWAYOS: usb0: ready
NOWAYOS: usb1: starting
NOWAYOS: usb1: controller identified
NOWAYOS: usb1: halted and reset
NOWAYOS: usb1: running: a No Op command came back through DMA
NOWAYOS: usb1: ready

# Output that fails the test at once if it appears anywhere (substring match):
# a fault reported by the Microkit monitor, a kernel error message, a panic,
# or a PD giving up.
!MON|ERROR
!seL4(CPU
!panicked
!gave up
